WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.300
In this video which is part of the greater
project revolution we’re going to be talking

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.450
about the Mexican war of independence in the
early 19th century.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:20.390
However before we start talking about the
Mexican war of independence or more accurately

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:22.020
the Wars of independence.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.560
We have to understand the social, political,
economical and religious aspects that drove

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.540
the Mexican ideas of revolution in the first
place.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:32.680
And for that we’ll have to look at the Viceroyalty
of New Spain.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:37.650
Also known as the Colony of New Spain.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:42.220
This colony was governed in all administrative
aspects by the Viceroy, who was appointed

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:43.710
by the Spanish monarch.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:48.260
The Viceroy was supposed to govern a colony
which at its largest extended included Southern

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:53.700
Canada, Venezuela, the Philippines, Florida,
etc. the pure scale of this colony meant that

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:58.040
the Viceroy couldn’t really govern the entire
viceroyalty effectively and therefore most

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:02.040
of the administrative and judicial matters
fell to the local governmental bodies, the

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.660
largest of which where the audiencias.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:07.540
There’s way more political organization
in New Spain then we have time to get in to

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:12.390
but some important things of note are that
the audiencias had to not only answer directly

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:15.930
to the viceroy but also the council and minister
of the indies.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:19.429
However this was only in administrative matters
not judicial ones.

00:01:19.429 --> 00:01:23.680
Plus the audiencias weren't even the only
governmental body, as there were smaller ones

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:28.190
called cabildo, intendencies, captaincies
general, etc.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:31.720
Lastly what is important to understand, is
that even though this was the ViceRoyalty

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:36.600
of New Spain at its largest extent, the borders
often changed and the viceroy control in some

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.280
border regions was purely superficial.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:45.040
This vast colony was governed from the former
aztec capital Tenochtitlan now renamed Mexico

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.040
City.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:50.380
Mexico City was not only the administrative
heartland of New Spain but also the economical

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:51.380
and social one.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:55.260
It was the largest city in the Western Hemisphere
in the 18th century and was connected from

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:59.990
the pacific by the port of Acapulco and the
Caribbean by the Port of Veracruz.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:04.650
This trade network going across the heartland
of Mexico created drastic economic development

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:08.730
within the area which resulted in the fact
that by the 18th century, the lands between

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:14.290
Veracruz, Mexico City and Acapulco had over
half of the entire population of New Spain.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:18.890
However this population of New Spain was very
heavily divided in to a casta system.

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:24.180
This system assigned social, economic, administrative
and other privileges to people depending on

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.629
their racial background.

00:02:25.629 --> 00:02:30.840
Now this system in its purest form was very
simple but in practice it was anything but

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:31.840
simple.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:37.080
It also changed drastically since the foundation
of new spain in 1521 until the early 19th

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:38.080
century.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:41.720
With that said I am going to be presenting
the casta system as it existed in the late

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:42.989
18th century.

00:02:42.989 --> 00:02:45.049
So the simple system went like this.

00:02:45.049 --> 00:02:49.920
On top where the peninsulares, people born
in Spain or elsewhere in Europe.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.799
This group had the largest social and economic
benefits and almost all high ranking administrative

00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:58.550
and governmental jobs in the colony could
be held by only them.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:03.550
Under Peninsulares were the Criollos, which
were people born to both Spanish or european

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.640
parents in the Americas.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:10.760
Criollos mostly had the same benefits as Peninsulares
with the exception that they could only be

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.670
appointed to lower level governmental jobs.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.930
Under the Criollos were mostly two classes.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.810
The Indios or Amerindians and the Mestizos.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:23.640
The Indios where people purely descended from
the native Indian population, and in fact

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:29.019
some amerindian communities where very strict
in the notion of pure blood Indios.

00:03:29.019 --> 00:03:33.340
It is very hard to classify this group because
their social status was very heavily dependent

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:34.999
on the families background.

00:03:34.999 --> 00:03:39.639
For example the Aztec nobility that existed
prior to the Spanish colonization got pretty

00:03:39.639 --> 00:03:42.200
much assimilated into the Spanish nobility.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:47.230
On top of that some Indios people became very
wealthy through mine or farm ownership and

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:50.629
those people enjoyed a very high standard
within the society.

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:55.549
With that said most of the indios people in
Mexico where poor peasants that were not allowed

00:03:55.549 --> 00:03:59.969
to hold any administrative jobs other than
in specifically defined amerindian communities.

00:03:59.969 --> 00:04:05.620
The Mestizos where people descended from one
Indios parent and one Spanish/European parent.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:11.400
In the early colonial era this term was associated
with being a bastard as Mestizos where oftentimes

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:16.430
born out of wedlock however in the late 18th
century the term started to be much more widespread

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:22.130
and started to encompass more racial subdivisions
then just purely having one indios and one

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.450
european parent.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:27.880
By the 19th century the word Mestizo started
to be used to describe any kind of a mixed

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:28.970
race person.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:34.370
Mestizos as Indios are hard to classify as
depending on their wealth, family history,

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:39.979
and sometimes just purely skin color, they
could have benefits as high as of a Criollo.

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:44.849
Under Indios and Mestizos were Mulatos, which
were people of european and African descended,

00:04:44.849 --> 00:04:48.449
and later also included people of Amerindian
and African descent.

00:04:48.449 --> 00:04:52.960
These people where at the low end of the casta
system not having any real benefits and if

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:56.599
their mom was a slave they could also end
up being slaves.

00:04:56.599 --> 00:04:59.539
Lastly where the Negros, people of pure African
decent.

00:04:59.539 --> 00:05:03.780
These people were mostly slaves or descendants
of slaves brought to New Spain mainly during

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:09.310
the 17th century, when Spain ruled over Portugal
and its vast Portuguese slave trade.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:13.050
However it is interesting to note that even
though legal by the late 18th century slave

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:17.651
ownership was almost non existent and the
population of Africans in mainland of New

00:05:17.651 --> 00:05:19.880
Spain was no more than 0.2%.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:23.729
This was mostly because by the end of the
18th century there was an abundance of cheap

00:05:23.729 --> 00:05:26.690
labor, mainly from the growing mestizo class.

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:30.560
This combined with the fact that mainland
New Spain had mostly higher profit margin

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:36.720
jobs like the textile industry, the die industry,
mining, etc. meant that slavery was largely

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:37.720
obsolete.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:41.290
The last important driving force in New Spain
was Catholicism.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:45.840
The Spanish inquisition was in full force
back in Europe and that mentality got very

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:50.860
much transferred over in to New Spain creating
what we now call the Mexican Inquisition.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:55.360
The Mexican inquisition was focused heavily
on converting the larger native population

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:56.610
in to Catholicism.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:06:00.790
The amerindians prior to the spanish arrival
had religion at the center of their society

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:04.539
and with their conversion to Catholicism this
did not change.

00:06:04.539 --> 00:06:09.389
Even though in many areas this conversation
was forceful, ones converted the native population

00:06:09.389 --> 00:06:13.909
became devout catholics that brought in many
aspects from their old religions.

00:06:13.909 --> 00:06:18.289
There’s no better example of this then the
apparition of the Virgin Mary to an Indios

00:06:18.289 --> 00:06:22.819
farmer in the 16th century, now known as our
Lady of Guadeloupe.

00:06:22.819 --> 00:06:27.020
The lady of Guadeloupe would later become
a symbol for the mestizo and amerindian parts

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:28.389
of the revolution.

00:06:28.389 --> 00:06:32.510
This new found avid devotion to catholicism
by the native population combined with the

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:37.690
already existing avid devotion to catholicism
of the spanish, meant that the Catholic church

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:42.940
had almost just the same amount of power in
New Spain as the Spanish monarchy itself.

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:49.080
These three pillars of New Spain; governance,
religion and the casta system where the major

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:54.150
forces behind the way the Mexican war of independence
started and finished.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:07:00.580
It all began during the Burbon reforms of
the 18th century when the new Burbon dynasty

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:05.639
in Spain hoped to reform their overseas territories
to bring new prosperity to their country.

00:07:05.639 --> 00:07:09.949
These reforms were focused on centralizing
the administration of the colonies, reaffirming

00:07:09.949 --> 00:07:14.629
more direct Spanish control over the colonies
and diminishing the power of the church.

00:07:14.629 --> 00:07:18.500
However what the reforms ended up doing was
giving even more power to the Peninsulares

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:22.840
making the Criollos and Mestizos unhappy and
also making enemies with the church which

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:27.889
would later on make it more sympathetic towards
the mexicans during their strive for independence.

00:07:27.889 --> 00:07:32.611
As animosity against spain grew in all the
social classes except the Peninsulare, the

00:07:32.611 --> 00:07:37.550
ideas of a revolution became more and more
prominent within the mexican people.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:42.439
All it needed now was a spark to light the
fire, and this spark came in a form of an

00:07:42.439 --> 00:07:45.490
averagely tall Frenchman called Napoleon.

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:52.150
Napoleon’s peninsular war which started
in 1807 was very messy and after the 1808

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:57.460
forced abdication of the Spanish monarch,
destroyed any Spanish control in the new world.

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:02.270
Almost immediately after the abdication multiple
Juntas where created throughout spain, each

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:06.500
claiming to be the legitimate representation
of the Spanish government and its king.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:11.039
These Juntas then sent out representatives
to the Spanish colonies, asking to be officially

00:08:11.039 --> 00:08:12.660
recognized by them.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:16.950
After receiving two representatives from two
different Spanish Juntas, the current Viceroy

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:20.889
of New Spain José de Iturrigaray, was very
confused.

00:08:20.889 --> 00:08:25.860
Nonetheless this arrival of multiple representative
proved to everyone that Spain had no real

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:31.080
control over New Spain anymore, and so the
debate about what to do next started.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:35.460
The Criollo party, which controlled the Mexico
City council, voted for self governance with

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:37.470
the current viceroy at its head.

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:43.270
Iturrigaray agreed as he was mostly a criollo
sympathizer and also would get to rule New

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:44.270
Spain.

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:47.660
However the Peninsulares who controlled the
audiencias vetoed this idea, arguing that

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:52.910
New Spain was a colony and therefor did not
have the right to self govern without Spain.

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:57.400
The peninsulares started to fear that their
control of New Spain was fading in favor of

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:02.220
the Criollos and therefor created a coup against
Iturrigaray, arresting him on some dubious

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:06.040
charges and quickly appointing one of their
own as a new Viceroy.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:10.600
For the next year Pedro de Garibay acted as
the Viceroy of the colony for all intensive

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.720
purposes as if nothing was happening in Spain.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:18.320
After a year he recognized the Spanish Junta
of Aranjuez whom mostly managed centralize

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:23.540
their power within Spain, and then he decided
to retire as he may have thought things bigger

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:26.000
than him where brewing across the colony.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:30.570
He appointed Francisco Javier as his successor
but this guy also lasted only a year after

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:32.730
being replaced by the Junta of Aranjuez.

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:38.280
The new Viceroy Francisco Javier Venegas was
sent from Spain to quel now the extremely

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:40.520
unhappy population of New Spain.

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:44.960
This is because ever since the coup by the
Peninsulares against Iturrigaray most Mexicans

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:49.120
felt like they were forcefully controlled
by the unlawful government in mexico city

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:52.130
which seldomly cared for the people of New
Spain.

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:56.470
And this idea was the battle cry for the first
Mexican independence movement that started

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:59.270
just 2 days after Venegas took office.

00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:03.461
Miguel Hidalgo y Costilla was the leader of
this movement starting in the town of Dolores.

00:10:03.461 --> 00:10:08.380
The revolutionary army was small at first
numbering only around 600 men but the next

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:12.880
few days they traveled across the Mexican
countryside killing any Peninsulares they

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:16.720
came across and gaining much needed support,
equipment and manpower.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:21.090
They also adopted the standard of the Virgin
of Guadalupe which would draw in much needed

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.940
Mestizo and Indios support for the revolution.

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:28.090
By the time the Viceroy was able to muster
up some sort of an army for defence Hidalgo

00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:31.250
had around 100,000 men at his disposal.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:35.580
Hidalgo met the much smaller New Spain's army
at the battle of Monte de las Cruces where

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:37.660
they scored a decisive victory.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:42.400
Now with the Mexico city within their sight
Hidalgo made a decision that has puzzled historian

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:43.660
to this day.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:48.570
He decided not to besiege Mexico city and
instead marched north towards the second most

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:51.270
important city in Mexico, Guadalajara.

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:55.630
Many of his troops disagreed with this choice
and started to deseret in mass.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:11:00.310
Ones he arrived to Guadalajara his army numbered
only around 6000 men.

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:04.520
None the less he manage to take the city and
gained support from the cities lower classes

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:06.370
and the surrounding countryside.

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:11.370
By the time the new Viceroyal army arrived
to Guadalajara Hidalgo had again around 80

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:12.830
to 100 thousand men.

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:17.860
However the army was ill equipped and therefore
was decisively defeated at the battle of Calderon

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:18.860
Bridge.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:23.450
After this defeat the revolutionaries tried
to flee towards the US but were later captured

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:28.800
and executed along with Hidalgo and with that
the Hidalgo’s independence movement was

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:29.800
over.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:32.380
However the revolution itself was far from
over.

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:36.661
The Peninsular abuse along with Hidalgos show
that the Spanish Could be defeated, meant

00:11:36.661 --> 00:11:40.460
that many new insurgencies spurred up all
around New Spain.

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:44.750
Ignacio López Rayón in the center of the
country Father José María Morelos in the

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:48.160
south and various other groups all around
the Colony.

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:51.820
But all these groups weren’t united in their
pursuit for freedom.

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:56.400
Some wanted the status quo unchanged other
then having Mexico not be under spanish control

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:01.370
anymore and others wanted a full change of
the Mexican hierarchy, administrative system,

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:03.140
policies and religion.

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:08.090
Therefore it is unsurprising that due to such
disunity and difference of ideas the Mexican

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:17.140
revolution continued in a stalemate until
1820 but what actually happened then?

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:22.800
Well in 1820 after a decade of fighting the
various Mexican insurgencies where on the

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:28.310
brink of collapse, mostly due to the now apathetic
stans of the Mexican people which were sick

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.990
of fighting at this point.

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:36.230
But in comes Agustín Cosme Damián de Iturbide
y Arámburu a Mexican nobleman who in 1820

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:40.040
was a royalist a colonel and a General of
South of New Spain.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:44.250
However despite his current status Iturbide
was a complicated man.

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:49.570
He was always a conservative sympathetic to
the royalists but he was also a criollo meaning

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:54.390
that throughout his life and military carrier
he faced setbacks due to the New Spain’s

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:55.390
casta system.

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:59.110
He was also asked by Hidalgo in the first
wave of the revolution to be a commander in

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:00.110
his army.

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:04.870
Iturbide however declined later joining the
royalists and fighting many of the insurgencies

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:06.550
of the 1810s.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:11.140
From the victories he gained during this time
Iturbide garnered much prestige and support

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:13.490
of the more conservative Mexicans.

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:18.540
But by 1820 even Iturbide started to be fed
up with the entire war and the Peninsular

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:20.190
control of the government.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:26.170
Plus being a conservative and a royalist when
Iturbide learned of a successful liberal revolution

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:30.870
in Spain which established a constitutional
monarchy, he just as many other conservative

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:36.180
Mexicans was afraid of what liberal changes
that would bring to a Monarchy centric New

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:37.180
Spain.

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:41.110
So when Iturbide was sent on what was suppose
to be the last royalist campaign against the

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:46.610
wavering revolutionaries, instead of fighting
them he attended a meeting with the insurgency

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:48.600
leader Vicente Guerrero.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:53.630
It was even at this first meeting that signs
of problems started to appear.

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:58.730
Iturbide representing the Mexican conservative
values wanted a Monarchy with the aristocracy

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:02.941
on top, an independent Mexican Monarchy but
a monarchy nonetheless.

00:14:02.941 --> 00:14:08.180
The revolutionaries on the other hand where
mostly republicans, hoping to establish a

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:09.910
USA like republic.

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:14.070
This divide was eventually settled by the
three guarantees.

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:18.750
First the newly independent Mexico will become
a monarchy under a Spanish or any other European

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:23.600
monarch that is willing to take the throne
but it will be a constitutional monarchy decided

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:25.740
upon to appease the liberals.

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:29.930
Second the aristocracy would still exist under
the Mexican Monarchy but the casta system

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:34.190
would be abolished, with all Mexican people
counted as equals.

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:37.940
Lastly to appease the conservatives and the
church the Catholic religion would become

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:41.930
the official and only religion of the new
Mexican Empire.

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:46.580
With this agreement which guaranteed the status
qou to be mostly unchanged for the higher

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:50.850
class and equality with representation in
the constitutional monarchy for the lower

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:56.710
class, for the first time in the Mexican revolution
most of the people were behind the same cause.

00:14:56.710 --> 00:15:01.510
So the revolutionary armies and the royalist
armies under Iturbide combined forming the

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:03.890
army of the three Guarantees.

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:09.040
This army then marched towards mexico city
where it was greeted by a joyce papules shouting

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:10.040
Viva Iturbide!

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:15.320
Seeing the videranging support for the three
guarantees the Viceroy along with the few

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:21.420
remaining people still loyal to Spain escaped
and with that the Empire of Mexico was proclaimed

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:22.760
in 1821.

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:28.440
Iturbide managed to achieve what 11 years
of senseless fighting didn’t.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:35.240
By compromising he manage to bring together
two main opposing factions and oust the Spanish.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:40.000
He was hailed all around Mexico and was given
the leadership role of the regency while a

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:44.120
suitable Spanish or European nobel was searched
for.

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:48.530
However no European noble wanted to take the
spot of Emperor of Mexico.

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:57.830
(wait what why sounds like a great job, I
would take it) Well this was because back

00:15:57.830 --> 00:16:02.990
in Spain the victorious liberals manage to
become the defeated liberals with the Spanish

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:04.380
Monarch regaining control.

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:08.580
He then set out to campaign against any other
European nobled taking the Mexican throne

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:11.970
and even had plans of invading Mexico himself.

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:16.870
The Mexican regency had no choice but to appoint
a Mexican noble on the throne.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:24.490
And no Mexican noble was as famous or as well
regarded as Iturbide, so in 1822 allegedly

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:30.870
against his wishes iturbide was crowned as
Emperor Agustín I of Mexico.

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:33.910
Iturbide however was facing problems right
from the get go.

00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:38.760
For example the conservative leaning areas
in Mexico still abided by the now technically

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:43.290
abolished casta system and the proclaimed
equality of the three guarantees wasn’t

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:44.880
really much existent.

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:49.160
Iturbide tried doing something against this
but that only lost him support with the hardline

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:54.880
conservatives which wanted the casta system,
on top of that he also lost support with the

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:59.350
royalists as they wanted a normal monarchy
not a constitutional one and also wanted a

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:02.060
european Monarch not a Mexican one.

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:06.110
On the other side of the political spectrum
Iturbide was hated by the republicans for

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:10.430
well existing as they wanted a republic not
monarchy.

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:14.600
Plus they thought he wasn’t doing enough
to enforce the abolishment of the casta system.

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:18.870
To add to all these problems Iturbide even
though a skilled general proved not to be

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:21.520
a skilled administrator or a politician.

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:27.390
Due to all this just a year later in 1823
the Republicans managed to gain control and

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:33.690
the sad and dimorelized Iturbide abdicated
after which he was exiled by the republicans.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:38.019
When Iturbide was leaving the country it was
still very clear that even though the far

00:17:38.019 --> 00:17:43.520
right and far left hated him he was still
loved by the majority of the country.

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:48.730
People gathered around his coach as he was
leaving and even insisted on pushing it themselves

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:50.299
instead of the horses.

00:17:50.299 --> 00:17:53.090
When he came to the coast he left for Italy.

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:55.919
During his exile the situation in Mexico worsen.

00:17:55.919 --> 00:18:00.399
The conservatives and royalists where in an
uproar as the republicans were in control.

00:18:00.399 --> 00:18:04.960
The republicans themselves were divided unable
to create a cohesive governmental body that

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:10.039
would succeed the Empire and the southern
states of Mexico proclaimed independence creating

00:18:10.039 --> 00:18:12.690
the united provinces of central america.

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:16.710
On top of all this the lower classes and the
far right liberals which up until now where

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:22.279
mostly controlled by the higher classes which
where mostly wealthy conservative Peninsulares,

00:18:22.279 --> 00:18:25.070
started to actively barade and attack them.

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:29.759
This meant that many wealthy Peninsulares
and even some Criollos started to leave for

00:18:29.759 --> 00:18:32.230
europe taking their wealth with them.

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:37.509
This wealth drain would continue for most
of the 19th century and arguably Mexico would

00:18:37.509 --> 00:18:39.130
never recover from it.

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:45.230
In all this chaos the royalists convince Iturbide
to return to Mexico and restore order.

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:51.440
He did in 1824 but the wavering royalist party
along with many of the people that would support

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:56.720
him now leaving to Europe meant that he wasn’t
able to garner much political support and

00:18:56.720 --> 00:18:57.720
power.

00:18:57.720 --> 00:19:02.129
None the less he was still loved by the majority
of the people and the republicans basically

00:19:02.129 --> 00:19:06.460
in a panic fearing an Iturbide takeover ordered
his execution.

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:12.169
Iturbide probably sick of fighting and not
wanting to cause another war which could destroy

00:19:12.169 --> 00:19:15.539
Mexico even more, surrendered peacefully.

00:19:15.539 --> 00:19:21.789
Many people called him incompetent, corrupt,
dictatorial, etc. and even though those words

00:19:21.789 --> 00:19:29.780
usually where well founded, he always tried
putting Mexico first, for better or for worse.

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:35.909
His last words before a firing squad where,
"Mexicans!

00:19:35.909 --> 00:19:43.610
In the very act of my death, I recommend to
you the love to the fatherland, and the observance

00:19:43.610 --> 00:19:47.330
to our religion, for it shall lead you to
glory.

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:54.650
I die having come here to help you, and I
die merrily, for I die amongst you.

00:19:54.650 --> 00:20:01.540
I die with honor, not as a traitor; I do not
leave this stain on my children and my legacy.

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:07.760
I am not a traitor, no."

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:14.080
Even after his death he was admired and respected
by most Mexicans and his life and demise represented

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:18.950
perfectly the dichotomy of Mexican politics
for the next 100 years.

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:28.870
With Mexico and its people going back and
forth between dictators and monarchs and republics.

